## Displays the filter picker of a Records table: one item per field=value constraint.
##
## Like the columns and sort pickers, this one gets its candidates from the browser, because they depend on the
## sibling class parameter and no displayer can be told about it. The element carries a class of ours rather than
## xwiki-selectize, so that this module owns the enhancement, and the bundle is loaded as a classic script, because
## the macro editor injects this template with jQuery. templates/html_displayer/recordscolumns/edit.vm explains each
## of these in full.
##
## Unlike those two pickers, this one is a text input rather than a multiple select. The parameter separates its
## constraints with &, but when the macro editor finds a field holding several values it joins them with a comma.
## With a single text input, the suggest widget writes the &-separated string itself, so the editor reads one
## value back and stores it unchanged. Reopening works the same way in reverse: the editor sets the stored string
## as the input value and the widget splits it on &. The widget learns its delimiter in JavaScript.
##
## An empty input submits an empty value, so removing every filter clears the parameter. That is why the hidden
## input #suggestInput adds after a multiple select is not needed here.
#set ($parameters = {})
#set ($discard = $parameters.putAll($displayer.parameters))
#set ($discard = $parameters.put('class', "$!parameters.get('class') suggest-records-filters"))
#set ($discard = $parameters.putIfAbsent('placeholder',
  $services.localization.render('rendering.macro.records.parameter.filters.placeholder')))
<script src="$escapetool.xml($services.webjars.url(
  'org.xwiki.platform:xwiki-platform-records-webjar', 'index.es.js'))"></script>
<input type="text" value="$!escapetool.xml($displayer.value)"
  #foreach ($parameter in $parameters.entrySet())
    $escapetool.xml($parameter.key)="$!escapetool.xml($parameter.value)"
  #end
/>
